/-- 32:X7 (p32033) — \textbf{The merging-cluster lensing offset} is a selection: the coherence-weighted enhancement follows the collisionless galaxies and drops the shock-decohered gas ($C_{ij}\to0$), not a coincidence. -/
theorem p32033 : (∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] (z : FRC.Shell p) (m : Nat), FRC.Shell.sumRange (fun x => z) m = FRC.Shell.ofNat m * z) ∧ (∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] {κ : Nat} {g : FRC.Shell p}, FRC.Shell.Frame p κ g → ∀ {x : FRC.Shell p} (n : Nat), x ^ n = (1 : FRC.Shell p) → x ≠ (1 : FRC.Shell p) → FRC.Shell.sumRange (fun l => x ^ l) n = (0 : FRC.Shell p)) ∧ ∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] (s1 s2 s3 : FRC.Shell p), (s1 + s2 + s3) * (s1 + s2 + s3) = s1 * s1 + s2 * s2 + s3 * s3 + (s1 * s2 + s1 * s2 + (s1 * s3 + s1 * s3) + (s2 * s3 + s2 * s3)) :=
  @FRC.Ledger.p32033
/-- 32:X8 (p32034) — \textbf{The cluster-core residual} is referred to the coherent amplitude addition $\sqrt{N_{\mathrm{eff}}}$ over the core's separately virialised composites, the one law that also gives the merger selection (C10); the quantitative closure, with $N_{\mathrm{eff}}$ uncomputed, is the conjecture Y1. -/
theorem p32034 : (∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] (s1 s2 s3 : FRC.Shell p), (s1 + s2 + s3) * (s1 + s2 + s3) = s1 * s1 + s2 * s2 + s3 * s3 + (s1 * s2 + s1 * s2 + (s1 * s3 + s1 * s3) + (s2 * s3 + s2 * s3))) ∧ ∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] (s : FRC.Shell p) (N : Nat), FRC.Shell.sumRange (fun x => s) N * FRC.Shell.sumRange (fun x => s) N = FRC.Shell.ofNat N * FRC.Shell.sumRange (fun x => s * s) N :=
  @FRC.Ledger.p32034
/-- 32:P5 (p32042) — Coherence-state cluster gas: the X-ray gas gravitates only when bulk-coherent, contributing in a relaxed cluster ($C_{ij}\to1$) and dropping out of a merger ($C_{ij}\to0$), the lensing displacement growing with the shock Mach number; the quantitative core residual of the same law is the conjecture Y1. Falsifier: a merger lensing peak tracking the shocked gas, or no relaxed-versus-merging difference. -/
theorem p32042 : (∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] (s1 s2 s3 : FRC.Shell p), (s1 + s2 + s3) * (s1 + s2 + s3) = s1 * s1 + s2 * s2 + s3 * s3 + (s1 * s2 + s1 * s2 + (s1 * s3 + s1 * s3) + (s2 * s3 + s2 * s3))) ∧ ∀ {p : Nat} [FRC.Pos p] (z : FRC.Shell p) (m : Nat), FRC.Shell.sumRange (fun x => z) m = FRC.Shell.ofNat m * z :=
  @FRC.Ledger.p32042
